replace("docs/design/s03-8.md", "\u2022 The session token travels where a token travels: Authorization: Bearer on REST and the first auth frame on /ws and /ws/tick. A session that is expired or revoked, or whose operator is disabled, gives 401 on REST and close 4401 on the sockets, and the dashboard clears sessionStorage and localStorage and shows Login.\n\u2022 The dashboard keeps the session token in sessionStorage, or in localStorage when \"remember me\" is ticked (off by default). INIT_AUTH to the Web Worker is unchanged.\n\u2022 No new error code and no new WebSocket message.\n", "\u2022 The session token travels where a token travels: Authorization: Bearer on REST and the first auth frame on /ws and /ws/tick. A session that is expired or revoked, or whose operator is disabled, gives 401 on REST and close 4401 on the sockets, and the dashboard clears sessionStorage and localStorage and shows Login.\n\u2022 The dashboard keeps the session token in sessionStorage, or in localStorage when \"remember me\" is ticked (off by default). INIT_AUTH to the Web Worker is unchanged.\n\u2022 No new error code and no new WebSocket message.\n\nREPLAY pause addendum (ADR 0061, Proposed; Rev 3.45 itself is unchanged)\n\u2022 POST /api/replay/pause \u2014 Req: {paused: bool} -> 200 {paused, finished} (sets the state, it does not toggle: asking for the state the replay already has changes nothing and writes no row; the first change logs REPLAY_PAUSE or REPLAY_RESUME; any logged-in operator may call it; pausing stops the scaled clock, so every timer of the host stops with the replay) | 401/403 | 409 (RECOVERING before the replay has started, retry_after_s = recovering_target_s; or STATE_CONFLICT on a host that is not in mode REPLAY and on a replay that has finished) | 422 (a body without a boolean paused). The call is the fourteenth endpoint of the list.\n\u2022 The snapshot and the system message carry replay: {speed: int, paused: bool, finished: bool}, or null when the host is not in mode REPLAY. A change of paused or finished sends a system message (at once for a pause or resume; with the next 1 Hz tick for the end of the data). The field is optional for a client: a message without it means a host that is not replaying.\n\u2022 No new error code and no new WebSocket message. Migration 0004 adds the two audit actions (audit_actions has 23 rows).\n");
